"helpText" = "## Using the Palette\n1. Choose Bracket palette from the （） menu bar item, or press **⌥⇧⌘U**.\n2. Select text in a field of the target app.\n3. Click a palette button.\n- The palette targets the app active when summoned. It does not take focus from the target app.\n- It hides when another app becomes active. Summon it again to target the new app.\n- Widening the window adds columns without widening buttons.\n- Palette mode (show palette on normal launch) keeps the target app focused. Size and position are saved. Hidden at login.\n\n## Converting Brackets\n### Supported Pairs\n- （） ［］ 【】 〈〉 《》 「」 ｛｝ 『』 “” ‘’\n- () [] {} <> ' ' \" \"\n- HTML comments <!-- --> and CSS comments /* */\n### Replacing and Wrapping\n- Existing outermost brackets in the selection are replaced; nested brackets remain. Unmatched and mixed delimiters are supported.\n- Multiple outer groups in the selection are replaced together. Reversed curly quotes at the selection edges are corrected.\n- Apostrophes inside words are not delimiters.\n- Without brackets, the selected text is wrapped. Without a selection, a pair is inserted and the caret is placed inside.\n- Text remains selected after editing.\n### Removing, Spaces and Outer Pairs\n- Remove outer brackets removes one outer level; Remove all brackets removes nested levels too.\n- Add surrounding spaces inserts one ASCII space on each side.\n- Always add an outer pair preserves existing brackets and wraps the entire selection.\n- HTML/CSS comments always wrap; comment syntax is not parsed or removed.\n- Trim ASCII spaces is off by default. It removes spaces adjacent to converted delimiters only within the selection, or trims the selection edges when wrapping. Newlines, tabs and full-width spaces remain.\n### Notes\n- This is text processing, not code parsing. Angle signs in HTML and mathematics count as brackets. Select only the intended text.\n- Clipboard and excluded-app settings remain unchanged.\n\n## Keyboard Shortcuts\n### App Commands (While This App Is Active)\n- **⌘0**: Open Main Window\n- **⌘,**: Settings\n- **⌘W**: Close the window\n- **⌘M**: Minimize the window\n- **⌘?**: Help\n- **⌘Q**: Quit\n- Other apps keep their ⌘Q.\n### Article Shortcuts\n26 operations use the article’s US physical key positions; symbols name the keys before Shift. On JIS, record different keys in Settings as needed. Smart single quotes ‘’ have no article binding. + means forced wrapping independent of the global toggle.\n- **⇧⌘9**: （）\n- **⇧⌘[**: ［］\n- **⇧⌘=**: 【】\n- **⇧⌘]**: 〈〉\n- **⇧⌘\\**: 《》\n- **⇧⌘;**: 「」\n- **⇧⌘0**: ｛｝\n- **⇧⌘-**: 『』\n- **⇧⌘'**: “”\n- **⌥⇧⌘0**: ()\n- **⌥⇧⌘[**: []\n- **⌥⇧⌘]**: {}\n- **⌥⇧⌘.**: <>\n- **⌥⇧⌘;**: ' '\n- **⌥⇧⌘'**: \" \"\n- **⌃⌥⌘9**: （）+\n- **⌃⌥⌘[**: ［］+\n- **⌃⌥⌘;**: 「」+\n- **⌃⌥⌘]**: 〈〉+\n- **⌃⌥⌘\\**: 《》+\n- **⌃⌥⌘/**: CSS comment\n- **⌃⌥⌘0**: HTML comment\n- **⇧⌘Space**: Spaces\n- **⇧⌘Delete**: Remove outer\n- **⌥⇧⌘Delete**: Remove all\n- **⌥⇧⌘U**: Palette\n※The article layout is applied once at first launch, backing up previous bindings in preferences. Later customizations and cleared bindings persist. Reset uses the article defaults.\n### Shortcut Settings\n- Open Settings from the （） menu bar item. In Shortcuts, change, disable, pause or reset only the shortcut.\n- **Esc** cancels recording. Not all conflicts with other apps can be detected.\n- Excluded apps release the hotkey to the app. Removing an app from Excluded apps does not delete the app.\n\n## Startup, Background and Quitting\n- Startup & Background in Settings includes launch at login (off by default) and Accessibility settings. Login launch is silent.\n- Choose Menu Bar Settings… in the app menu, or Show in menu bar in Settings, to show or hide the （） menu bar item. Hiding it does not quit the app.\n- By default, closing windows leaves the menu bar app running. Reopen the app or use its menu for Settings.\n- Use “Keep running after closing” to switch this. It defaults to on and is saved.\n- When off, closing the last window quits the app and stops its hotkey. Switching it off does not immediately quit. An open Help or other window keeps the app running.\n- This setting is independent of launch at login. Login launches stay silent until you open a window; closing the last window then follows this setting.\n- To quit, press **⌘Q** while this app is active, or choose Quit KakkoReplace from the （） menu bar item.\n\n## Permissions and Compatibility\n- Accessibility is required to read and edit text and selection. Allow this app in System Settings. No editing occurs without permission. Full Disk Access is unnecessary.\n- Requires standard readable and writable accessibility text and selection attributes. Custom editors, web fields and Adobe apps may not support them.\n- Password and read-only fields are skipped.\n- Formatting preservation depends on the target app; use plain text.\n\n## Results and Recovery\n- Results appear in the menu and Settings. Errors beep.\n- Success requires reading back text and selection.\n- Restore last change restores only the latest edit, only if the original field still contains the expected result. Recovery is kept in memory until quit.\n- Target app Undo is not guaranteed.\n\n## Troubleshooting\n- If permission changes do not take effect, relaunch from the same location.\n- Commit IME composition before running.\n- Check the target app after partial failures.\n\n## Privacy, Removal and Updates\n- Local processing only. No network, text logging or clipboard access.\n- The last field text is held in memory for recovery and discarded at quit.\n- Settings persist. They use jp.local.SuperKakkoEdit UserDefaults.\n- To remove, disable login launch, quit and move the app to Trash.\n- Check for Updates… and Automatically Check for Updates in the app menu show that updates are not configured, and make no network access, until an update feed and signing key are set up. Notarization is not configured.\n\n## Support\n- For support, use the chat where this app was requested.\n- Open the note Article, in the Help menu or in Help under the （） menu bar item, opens Swwwitch’s note support magazine.";
